  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "perception and hidden objects",
  "premise": "A scout wants to identify a supposed giant after discovering an enormous three-toed print, but every proposed monster contradicts the next clue. The camera finally pulls back to show a tiny scout examining the end of a garden fork pressed into clay, and the scout updates the sketch to FORK.",
  "hook": "Whatever made this has three terrible toes.",
  "visible_action": "Scout measures the print; monster doodles grow; camera pulls back; a fork-shaped tool rests beside the matching clay impression.",
